    "done_when": "The review of an-unchanged-run-costs-one-stat (81, merged at 861df54cd) found the following in reckon/crew/recovery.py. _snapshot_reuse_key (about line 8235) does not cover stall_seconds. _refresh_snapshot (about line 8328) re-derives state from the entry's frozen snapshot['stall_window_seconds']. A caller that passes cache=None shares the module-level _SNAPSHOT_CACHE (about line 8275). So two callers with different stall windows over one unchanged run can get a stalled or working verdict measured against the other caller's window. The callers of _watch_snapshot are reckon/cli.py about line 2568, reckon/crew/recovery.py about lines 9075 and 9290, and reckon/crew/runs.py about line 1447. The node makes the reuse path recompute the stall window from the caller's stall_seconds through _stall_window_seconds, and leaves the reuse key unchanged. It names that choice in the commit body. A reused snapshot's state for a given stall_seconds must equal a full recompute's. tests/test_a_reused_snapshot_takes_the_callers_stall_window.py builds one unchanged run, takes a snapshot with a short window, then reads it through the shared cache with a long window, and the reverse. It asserts each state equals the full-recompute state for that window. The declared negative control is executed and logged. Base and head arms of tests/test_an_unchanged_run_costs_one_stat.py and tests/test_producer_reads_only_what_changed.py show zero added failures, each run with -n 8 in a git worktree or archive of its revision, each log naming its revision and ending in its pytest summary and EXIT= line. The manifest's baseline_suite and after_suite command fields carry the literal commands that ran.",
    "estimated_hours": 0.7,
